[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Dungeons and Dragons has enjoyed a resurgence in recent times. It\'s a world of fighters, sorcerers, elves and dwarves. In D&amp;D, dwarves are short of stature, but it seems that in Nordic mythology, they\'re huge. In particular, there are four dwarves in northern'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mythology that combine to hold up the sky. One in the north, one in the south, one in the east, and one in the west. And one of those four dwarves is called Vestry. And now the name of that giant is the name of another giant as well.'

[00:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; This is the $99 US'

[00:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Vestry dongle DAC and headphone amp from Shiit Audio. And I\'m not calling it a giant killer, I\'m just calling [music] it a giant. Let me explain. &gt;&gt; [music]'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Inside the Vestry is a regular old ES9018 DAC chip. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; And the amplifier in the Vestry is made of some regular old OPA1656 op amps. That\'s good for a dongle capable of'

[01:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'outputting 400 mW into a pair of 32 ohm headphones, which is great, [music] but it\'s hardly redefining anything. And then, there are the touch controls. The glass front of the Vestry allows for some touch sensitive zones under some of'

[01:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the buttons and the display lights. Those are at the end of the volume indicator bars to change the volume up and down. And in the center of the three icons that allow you to do things like change the phase of the signal, you can'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'toggle the non-oversampling mode on and off, and you can toggle the loudness mode. One quick tip here is that the touch zone for toggling the various options, the three options here, is right in the middle of those three'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'options. It is actually shown that way in the manual, but it didn\'t register properly in my brain. And so, once you know that you need to press the middle icon to activate the flashing, and then you can tap it again to move through the'

[02:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'options, you\'ll work it out for yourself once you know that where you need to touch is the middle icon, the one for the non-oversampling mode. That\'s the active part of the touch area. I struggled at first, but that\'s entirely on me. But, coming back to what I\'ve'

[02:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'been saying about this being a giant, those touch controls are nice, but they\'re hardly a game-changing feature. There\'s actually just one relatively tiny feature in the Vestry that changes everything. And I say tiny in the sense'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that it\'s often overlooked in these kinds of devices, but the impact that it has is absolutely huge. And what I\'m referring to is the very specific secret to Schiit Audio\'s Mesh DAC technology.'

[02:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And that specific secret is Schiit Audio\'s proprietary filter technology. That filtering works alongside that regular old ESS DAC chip that I mentioned before as being inside the'

[02:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Vestry, and it\'s what makes the Vestry something truly special. If you\'re not familiar with how all this Mesh DAC technology and filtering stuff works, basically, Schiit Audio have gone into the coding and the setup of the ESS DAC'

[03:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'chip inside the Vestry, and they\'ve switched off all of ESS\'s own filters. Instead, they\'re just using that ES9018 DAC chip to just decode from digital to analog. Whereas normally, a DAC chip'

[03:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'like that does a bunch of filtering as well. Instead, what they\'re doing by turning off that ESS filtering is then applying their own filters that Schiit Audio have developed over many, many years to do all of the heavy lifting.'

[03:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And what that particular approach does is output a signal with both fantastic frequency accuracy, but also very importantly, fantastic timing accuracy. And if we get beyond what all those'

[03:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'technical things actually mean, and really talk about what matters, which is the listening experience. It results in an incredibly [snorts] great sounding dongle DAC and headphone amp. In fact, when it comes down to it,'

[03:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I have only one issue with anything about the Vestry, and that is that there were a few occasions where I wished I could get just a slightly different volume level, either a tiny bit louder or a tiny bit softer. Unfortunately, the'

[04:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'way the Vestry is designed, you don\'t get any controls on your smartphone, even with an app like USB audio player pro. And so, all of the controls have to be done via the touch panel on or touch panels on the Vestry DAC. Very'

[04:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'occasionally, depending on the headphones I was listening to or the earphones I was listening to and the track that I was listening to, I very occasionally would find myself stuck where I just didn\'t quite get the right'

[04:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'volume level that I wanted, and the steps on the Vestry were just a little bit too big to ever get it quite right. I can\'t stress enough that it was only a very occasional thing, and it wasn\'t like it was massively wrong. I didn\'t'

[04:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have to go super loud or super soft. I just couldn\'t get it to exactly where I would have liked it for that particular track, earphone, or headphone. And so, that\'s my only gripe. It\'s a very tiny gripe, but it\'s one that I did want to mention. What was far more important to'

[05:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'me though, and what is far more important for me to share with you though, is just how good the Vestry sounds. Its tonality I would describe as very natural, and its sense of resolution I would describe as very good. Its sense of sound stage size and'

[05:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'separation is nothing short of grand for a dongle costing $99. For example, when I compared it to FiiO\'s KA15 dongle DAC that cost $95, its sound was decidedly inside my head'

[05:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'compared to the spacious and expansive Vestry sound. The Vestry was creating a lifelike sound stage experience. The KA15 was reminding me that I was'

[05:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'listening to headphones and earphones. I\'d say that the resolution and tonality from both devices was very similar. So, that\'s not really a reason to buy one over the other. But, the sound staging and separation of sounds is absolutely a'

[05:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reason to choose the Vestry. And so, knowing that the Vestry was clearly stronger than the FiiO K3 15, I decided to go up a step in FiiO\'s range because I had it on hand to the QX3 13. The QX3'

[06:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '13 cost more than twice the price of the Vestry, but the Vestry still sounded better. The Vestry was more spacious once again, but the QX3 13 probably did have an edge when it comes to'

[06:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'resolution. Or, perhaps it\'s just that the QX3 13\'s sound is a little bit more on the neutral or analytical side by a small margin, and that can sometimes make something sound a bit more resolving when it may actually not be.'

[06:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Either way, what mattered most to me was that going between the Vestry and the QX3 13, listening to the Vestry sounded like live music. Listening to the QX3 13 sounded like a fantastic recording and'

[06:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reproduction of live music. And so, I upgraded again. This time I reached for iFi\'s hip-dac 3, which costs $199, making it roughly twice the price of the'

[06:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Vestry, but it\'s a larger device with its very own battery supply, which I figured would make it a better sounding device. Another reason I reached for the hip-dac 3 was because it uses the Burr-Brown DAC chips. A DAC chip design'

[07:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that is often quite spacious and smooth sounding. And indeed, on this occasion, they did create a greater sense of space than what I tried before. And in that sense, they started to probably match what I was hearing from the Vestry.'

[07:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'However, to me, the Vestry now had an edge in resolution, and I think it was still separating sounds better as well, more clearly focusing them in space. And so, I upgraded again. This time I went to a full-sized desktop headphone amp'

[07:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and DAC, and it was the XDuoo XD-02. I never find that miniature portable devices sound as good as their equivalently priced desktop counterparts with full-size components, full-size'

[07:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'power supplies, and no limitations because they need to be tiny and portable. And it\'s true that the XD-02 did have an edge here. It was clearly more resolving than the Vestry. However, it\'s also true that the Vestry was'

[08:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'clearly more three-dimensional with a larger soundstage and better separation still. And the differences were large enough here that if I were choosing between the full-size desktop XD-02 and the Schiit Audio Vestry,'

[08:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'d just grab the Vestry at half the price and tiny in size. And by the way, all of that remains true whether you\'re using the 4.4 mil or the 3.5 mil output from the Vestry, it remains brilliant no'

[08:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'matter which output you\'re using. And that\'s why, not that about the 3.5 and the 4.4, but everything I\'ve said to you so far is why I said at the beginning that this is not a giant killer. This is'

[08:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just a giant. This is an incredible feat of product design that redefines value and sound quality in portable audio devices. And for the skeptics out there, I should let you know if you were to buy'

[08:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a FiiO QX-13 or KA15 or an XDuoo XD-02, I could make money from the affiliate links that I have for those products. I can make no money if you buy a Vestry.'

[09:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There are no affiliate programs with Schiit Audio and they don\'t pay for reviews. And yet, I am still highly recommending that you should go and buy the Schiit Audio Vestry if this is the type of product you\'re looking for. In'

[09:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'fact, I\'m recommending it so highly that I\'m also giving it the Passion for Sound Recommended Award because it is just such an incredibly great sounding DAC and headphone amp, &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; particularly at the price, but even if you forget about price. And so, as'

[09:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'always, you can use the link in the description below to pick up the Vestry for yourself and again I make no money from that. It\'s just a brilliant device. But if you\'re wondering why the Vestry is so good at this point, I\'ll pin a'

[09:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video here at the end of an interview I did with Jason Stoddard from Schiit Audio talking all about that mesh DAC technology and what makes [music] it so special. So watch that one next. But until next time, peace, love and music and I\'ll see you again soon.'
